  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Melissa** (1 review): The Dylan, Harrison, and Prince medley featuring this track is a highlight [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Blowin’ in the Wind**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [6]\n- **Melissa**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [6]\n- **All Things Must Pass**: rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmi2017-08-11.elam260.ck8.f8.flac** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 122 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **mmj2017-08-11.wklitz.neumannKM150.flac16**: source not stated; 17 songs; 121 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n- **mmj2017-08-11.km184.flac16**: source not stated; 17 songs; 124 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The reviewer noted the group functions as a rock band, not a jam band [5]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmi2017-08-11.elam260.ck8.f8.flac**: taped by Ted Gakidis; transferred by Ted Gakidis; source: Telefunken ELA M260/AKG ck8(PAS) > Zoom F8(24/48) [1]\n- **mmj2017-08-11.wklitz.neumannKM150.flac16**: taped by Keith Litzenberger; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Neumann KM150's>SDMP6 [2]. Also: Keith Litzenberger recorded using Neumann KM150 mics and a Sound Devices MixPre-6; Audio was processed in Nuendo and Sound Forge, then converted to 16-bit FLAC [2]\n- **mmj2017-08-11.km184.flac16**: taped by Justin Marinoff; source: Neumann km184 (ots/behind foh/ortf) > Sound Devices 722 (@24bit/48kHz) [3]",
